<title>JAPAN: Tokyo corn futures market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo corn futures market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo corn futures market is closed on Monday for a national holiday. Trading will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, most contracts of Tokyo corn futures market hit daily 400 yen limit-up at the closing. The benchmark January 1998 contract closed 400 yen higher at 14,620 yen per tonne.</p>
